    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d338">

                <pb facs="0428" n="324" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg324"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">733.35/25a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Argentina
                        (Bliss)</hi><anchor n="5" xml:id="d338-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-07-19T17:00:00-04:00">July 19, 1932—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>44. Department leaves to you and the Minister at Montevideo full discretion in
                    the matter of rendering good offices to Argentina and Uruguay and Depart, will
                    take no action except on your suggestion.</p>
                <p> Admiral Hamlet, Commandant of the Coast Guard, states that vessels may remain at
                    Montevideo if necessary for a week or 10 days after their scheduled departure on
                    July 20, and that the commanding officer, Commander Jones, has entire discretion
                    to comply with your request to that effect.</p>
                <p>Keep Department informed of developments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d338-f1" n="5" type="source" xml:id="d338-f1-content">
                <p>The same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, July 19, to the Minister
                    in Uruguay.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
